3. The brief facts of the present case are that on 30.08.2000, the Food Inspectors Sh. Jeet Ram and Sh. S.K. Gupta under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh. Satnam Singh reached at the premises M/s Balaji Sweet Corner at 128 Railway Road, Shahadra, Delhi-32, where accused/appellant was found conducting business of various food articles which were lying stored for sale for human consumption ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to purchase a sample of 'Burfee' from the vendor which was lying in open tray bearing no label declaration, to which he agreed ;
CA no. 56/17 Mukut Lal Vs. Vs. The State / DA - that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor/appellant and offer towards the sale price of sample to which he agreed and accepted the sale consideration, sample was then lifted ; that each sample was separately packed, fastened,
marked, sealed and necessary documents including Notice as per Form-VI in the presence of appellant/accused alongwith Panchnama etc was prepared at the spot ; the price of the sample commodity was paid to the vendor ;
- that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 15.09.2000, PA found the sample to be adulterated not conforming to the standards on the grounds that it contained vegetable oil which was not declared as an ingredient ;
- that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by Food Inspector and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.

